at":"2019-08-24T00:14:52Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T03:51:18Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T01:35:43Z","git_url":"git://github.com/streamlit/streamlit.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:streamlit/streamlit.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit","homepage":"https://streamlit.io","size":797696,"stargazers_count":42660,"watchers_count":42660,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3962,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1304,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["data-analysis","data-science","data-visualization","deep-learning","developer-tools","machine-learning","python","streamlit"],"visibility":"public","forks":3962,"open_issues":1304,"watchers":42660,"default_branch":"develop","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/pulls/537","html_url":"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/pull/537","diff_url":"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/pull/537.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/pull/537.patch","merged_at":"2019-10-29T23:52:26Z"},"body":"**Issue:** https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/366\r\n\r\n**Description:** \r\nThis is a sketch for now, we may want to look at a more sophisticated fix. Although it does fix the linked issue, it does so in a somewhat scorched-earth manner.\r\n\r\nEssentially what is happening is that if you have a module which is not directly imported by the base module (e.g.` app.py` imports `a.py`, `a.py` imports `b.py`), then changes to that module will not be reloaded when a file change is detected.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can understand, this is what is happening:\r\n- User changes `b.py`\r\n- Reload logic:\r\n  - Deletes `b` from `sys.modules`\r\n  - Calls eval on the code from `app.py`\r\n  - The code in `app.py` imports `a`, which is already present in `sys.modules`, and so we are done\r\n  - The result is that we keep using the old copy of `b` in memory until `a` is reloaded\r\n\r\nThe ideal solution would be to unload both the modified module, as well as any modules that are importing it, but determining this tree of all possible paths for importing a given module may not be worth the effort.\r\n\r\nInstead, what this PR does is simply unloads all watched modules. So in the scenario above, `a` gets unloaded as well when `b` changes, and so at the eval point both modules get reloaded, therefore reflecting the changes to `b` in the running app.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Contribution License Agreement**\r\n\r\nBy submiting this pull request you agree that all contributions to this project are made under the Apache 2.0 license.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/537/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2750178745,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3NTAxNzg3NDU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/events/2750178745","actor":{"login":"tvst","id":690814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDgxNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/690814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvst","html_url":"https://github.com/tvst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvst/gists{/gist